{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 25, :comments ["<b>And it came to pass on the third day, when they were in pain.</b> It is astonishing: what did they see to act deceptively with the men of the city, to tell them to circumcise themselves and afterward kill them? One may say that they did not act deceptively, for on the third day they were in pain and were regretting the circumcision, and therefore they killed them. And it is astonishing why they waited until the third day, for one cannot say that they were in more pain on the third day than on the first and second. Rather, the reason appears to be that all the men of Shechem could not all be circumcised in one day, nor in two, and on the third day they were all in pain, for by then they had all already been circumcised: ״ויקחו איש חרבו״."], :book :genesis, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 34, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:06:28.432157756Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}